<article class="env-lemma" id="05PM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05PM">Lemma <span data-tag="05PM">19.9.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Cov} = \{ \{ f : V \to U\}  \mid f\text{ is surjective}\} .  \]
</div>
  <p> Then $(\mathcal{A}, \text{Cov})$ is a site, see Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/00VH" data-tag="00VH">7.6.2</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that $\mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{A})$ is a set by our conventions about categories. An isomorphism is a surjective morphism. The composition of surjective morphisms is surjective. And the base change of a surjective morphism in $\mathcal{A}$ is surjective, see Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/05PK" data-tag="05PK">12.5.14</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>